      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_attachments",
    "title": "List attachments",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List the owners’ answers that may be decisions",
    },
    "description": "Only the Operator, not in guest conversations; needs no open owner request. The questions an owner answered on cards since you last looked, which they have not given a verdict on yet, the earliest answer first. Offer them to the owner in your answer to their message; the call counts as a look, so the same answers come back only if you did not mark them. Refused with docs_not_configured when the project has no decision log. more true: there are further candidates, call again after marking these.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "limit": {
          "description": "How many to return, 1–50 (default 20).",
          "maximum": 50,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_decision_candidates",
    "title": "List the owners’ answers that may be decisions",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List team members",
    },
    "description": "List the team: handle, name, human or AI, role, status and current tasks. Use it to find the right teammate to address (by handle) and to see who is busy with what.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_members",
    "title": "List team members",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List tasks",
    },
    "description": "Read the project board as a compact list, newest update first. Defaults to open tasks (active, waiting or blocked). Filter by status, stage or assignee; use get_task for details. A theme (a card that groups other cards) is marked kind "theme"; it is in no stage, so a stage filter leaves themes out. A card in the project focus (what the team works on now) carries its place as "focus" (position, and via: the theme or card that covers it).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "assignee": {
          "description": "Member handle, or "me" for your own tasks.",
          "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "limit": {
          "default": 50,
          "maximum": 200,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "stage": {
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "status": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "const": "open",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "enum": [
                "active",
                "waiting",
                "blocked",
                "done",
                "cancelled",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
          ],
          "default": "open",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_tasks",
    "title": "List tasks",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Mark the offered decision candidates",
    },
    "description": "Only the Operator, in the owner's own conversation, during an open owner request. Record what the owner said about the candidates you offered: recorded (they said yes and the entry is in the decision log; decision is its number, 1–10 characters), declined (they said no: never offer it again) or skipped (not a decision). All or nothing: one unknown item_id refuses the whole call with not_found. An item already marked can be marked again when the owner asks.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "items": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "decision": {
                "description": "The decision log entry number; only with recorded.",
                "maxLength": 10,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "item_id": {
                "maxLength": 100,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "verdict": {
                "enum": [
                  "recorded",
                  "declined",
                  "skipped",
                ],
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "item_id",
              "verdict",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "maxItems": 50,
          "minItems": 1,
          "type": "array",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "items",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "mark_decision_candidates",
    "title": "Mark the offered decision candidates",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
